#: includes/Checks/BlacklistCheck.php:32
msgid "Server IP Blacklists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/BlacklistCheck.php:92
msgid "Skipped: your email is sent through an SMTP plugin or mail service, so your web server's own IP address is not what receivers see."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/BlacklistCheck.php:98
msgid "Skipped on the command line, where the web server's IP address is not available. Set it with the ecehc_server_ip filter to check it here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/BlacklistCheck.php:102
msgid "Your server's public IPv4 address could not be determined (it may be IPv6, private, or behind a proxy), so blacklists were not checked."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: server IP address, 2: list names
#: includes/Checks/BlacklistCheck.php:170
#, php-format
msgid "Your server IP address %1$s is listed on: %2$s. Mail sent straight from this server is likely to be rejected or sent to spam. Ask your host to resolve it, or send through an SMTP service instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/BlacklistCheck.php:178
msgid "The DNS lookups to the blacklists failed, so your server IP address could not be checked. Try again later."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: server IP address, 2: list names
#: includes/Checks/BlacklistCheck.php:185
#, php-format
msgid "Your server IP address %1$s is not listed on %2$s. Only these free lists are checked: major lists such as Spamhaus cannot be queried by a plugin under their terms, so a clean result here does not guarantee a clean reputation."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: check id
#: includes/Checks/CheckRunner.php:64
#, php-format
msgid "Duplicate diagnostic check id \"%s\" was skipped."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: domain of the From address
#: includes/Checks/CheckRunner.php:79
#, php-format
msgid "(Checked for %s, the domain of your From address.)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DkimCheck.php:25
msgid "DKIM Record"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: DKIM selector name
#: includes/Checks/DkimCheck.php:63
#, php-format
msgid "A DKIM key was found for selector \"%s\". This lets receivers verify that your emails were not altered."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DkimCheck.php:70
msgid "The DNS lookup was not possible on this server, so DKIM could not be checked. Use an online DKIM checker with your mail provider's selector."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DkimCheck.php:73
msgid "No DKIM key was found under common selectors. Your mail provider may use a custom selector that cannot be detected automatically. Check your provider's DNS instructions or use an online DKIM checker."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DmarcCheck.php:22
msgid "DMARC Record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DmarcCheck.php:35
msgid "The DNS lookup was not possible on this server, so the DMARC record could not be checked. Use an online DMARC checker for your domain."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DmarcCheck.php:44
msgid "A DMARC record was found, but its policy is \"none\" (monitoring only). Once your email is authenticated correctly, consider moving to \"quarantine\" or \"reject\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DmarcCheck.php:47
msgid "A DMARC record was found. This tells receiving servers how to treat email that fails authentication."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/DmarcCheck.php:50
msgid "No DMARC record was found. Without one, mailbox providers have no policy for spoofed or unauthenticated email from your domain, which can hurt deliverability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/PendingOrdersCheck.php:29
msgid "Unpaid Orders"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/PendingOrdersCheck.php:34
#: includes/Checks/PendingOrdersCheck.php:44
msgid "WooCommerce orders could not be read."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of unpaid or failed orders, 2: number of orders that went through
#: includes/Checks/PendingOrdersCheck.php:58
#, php-format
msgid "In the last 7 days, %1$d orders are still \"Pending payment\" or \"Failed\" against %2$d that went through (processing, completed or on hold). WooCommerce sends no order emails for unpaid orders, so customers may look like they are missing emails when the real cause is a payment problem. Check your payment gateway before changing your email setup."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of unpaid or failed orders, 2: number of orders that went through
#: includes/Checks/PendingOrdersCheck.php:69
#, php-format
msgid "In the last 7 days, %1$d orders are \"Pending payment\" or \"Failed\" and %2$d went through (processing, completed or on hold). WooCommerce sends no order emails for unpaid orders, so a few are normal (abandoned checkouts)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SenderAddressCheck.php:16
msgid "Sender Address Check"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: email address, 2: domain such as gmail.com
#: includes/Checks/SenderAddressCheck.php:28
#, php-format
msgid "Your emails are sent from %1$s. Receivers expect mail from %2$s to come from its own servers, so mail sent from your site is likely to be rejected or sent to spam. Use an address at your own domain instead."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: email address
#: includes/Checks/SenderAddressCheck.php:40
#, php-format
msgid "Your emails are sent from %s, whose domain matches your site domain. This is good practice."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: email address, 2: domain of the From address
#: includes/Checks/SenderAddressCheck.php:49
#, php-format
msgid "Your emails are sent from %1$s, whose domain differs from your site domain. That is fine if %2$s is a domain you control and your mail service is set up for it. The SPF, DKIM and DMARC checks below are run for %2$s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SmtpConfiguredCheck.php:22
msgid "SMTP / Mail Service"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SmtpConfiguredCheck.php:27
msgid "No SMTP plugin or mail service was detected, so WordPress is probably sending email through your web host's default PHP mail. That mail is unauthenticated and is often filtered as spam or blocked. Use an SMTP plugin or a transactional email service to send authenticated email."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: mail provider name, e.g. SendGrid, 2: plugin name(s)
#: includes/Checks/SmtpConfiguredCheck.php:39
#, php-format
msgid "Email appears to be sent through %1$s, handled by %2$s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: mail provider name, e.g. SendGrid
#: includes/Checks/SmtpConfiguredCheck.php:51
#, php-format
msgid "Email appears to be sent through %s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: plugin name(s)
#: includes/Checks/SmtpConfiguredCheck.php:62
#, php-format
msgid "Outgoing email is handled by: %s."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SmtpConfiguredCheck.php:68
msgid "A plugin or mail service that handles outgoing email was detected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:24
msgid "SPF Record Validation"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:29
msgid "Your server does not allow DNS lookups, so the SPF record could not be checked. Use an online SPF checker for your domain."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:41
msgid "The DNS lookup failed, so the SPF record could not be checked. Try again later or use an online SPF checker."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:52
msgid "Multiple SPF records were found. Only one is allowed (RFC 7208), and receivers will treat your SPF as invalid. Merge them into a single record."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:57
msgid "An SPF record exists but does not authorize any sending service (no include:, ip4:, ip6:, a, mx or redirect). Add the service that sends your email, such as your SMTP provider or host."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: mail service name
#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:66
#, php-format
msgid "A valid SPF record was found and it appears to include %s, the service your site sends email through."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: mail service name
#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:75
#, php-format
msgid "A valid SPF record was found. %s authenticates SPF through its own return-path records, so it does not need to appear in your root SPF record. Make sure you completed its domain setup."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %1$s: mail service name
#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:84
#, php-format
msgid "Your site sends email through %1$s, but your SPF record does not appear to include it. Add the include value from your provider's DNS instructions to your SPF record, or emails may fail SPF. (If %1$s is listed inside another include, you can ignore this.)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:90
msgid "A valid SPF record was found. This helps authenticate your emails. Make sure it includes the service that actually sends your mail."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Checks/SpfCheck.php:93
msgid "No SPF record was found. This is a critical issue that makes your emails look suspicious to spam filters."
msgstr ""

